  "description": "PROCESS-PF8-KEY at :257-274 with CDEMO-CT00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG at N, so 'IF NEXT-PAGE-YES' at :267 is false and PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD is never performed - no file operation of any kind, so there is no STARTBR, no READNEXT and no ENDBR to observe. The flag is trusted rather than re-derived, and it can only be trusted because the 88-levels at :67-68 sit on a field that lives inside the 58-byte commarea extension at :66: 'SET NEXT-PAGE-NO TO TRUE' at :99 is overwritten by the MOVE at :111, so the value actually tested is the one the client carried back from the look-ahead READNEXT at :308 on the previous pass - which is the whole reason that look-ahead exists, and the reason no server-side session is needed to remember it. Note the asymmetry with PF7 that this pair makes visible - PF7 sets NEXT-PAGE-YES unconditionally at :242 while PF8 changes no flag at all - and note that PF8 falls back to HIGH-VALUES at :260 where PF7 falls back to LOW-VALUES at :237. The message is the inline forty-four-character literal 'You are already at the bottom of the page...' at :270-271, space padded into the PIC X(80) WS-MESSAGE and then right-truncated into the PIC X(78) ERRMSGO at :531; it is NOT the CCDA-MSG-INVALID-KEY constant of app/cpy/CSMSG01Y.cpy, which belongs to the WHEN OTHER arm at :129-133 and therefore to a different case. 'SET SEND-ERASE-NO TO TRUE' at :272 selects the second SEND at :541-548, so the single send here is again without erase. No XCTL runs on this path: control falls through to 'EXEC CICS RETURN TRANSID' at :138-141, so no next program is named and CT00 simply re-drives itself, with every piece of conversation state travelling in the payload. WS-ERR-FLG is never written here - :97 leaves it off and nothing on this path sets it - so the refusal is observable only through the message text and the no-erase send: COTRN00C copies no CSSETATY and writes no attribute byte anywhere, so no colour and no '*' marker is expected on any field. The class is named TransactionMenuController, but the program header at :5 reads 'List Transactions from TRANSACT file' - it lists, it holds no menu option table, and the mandated name is honoured without being allowed to alter one expectation. Every value here was derived statically, by reading app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl against its copybooks, and was never captured from a running COBOL program.",
